+    /// Return trailers that have already been received and buffered internally,
+    /// without consuming them or waiting for the terminal QUIC stream FIN.
+    ///
+    /// `poll_recv_trailers` intentionally waits for FIN after receiving trailer
+    /// HEADERS so it can reject any known frame that arrives after trailers. Some
+    /// applications still need to recover already-buffered trailers when their
+    /// own post-body trailer wait deadline fires before that FIN; this method
+    /// exposes only the already-buffered trailer block and leaves normal stream
+    /// validation state untouched for callers that keep polling.
